<Solution>
  <Folder Name="/Dependencies/">
    <Project Path="libs/Hermod/Hermod/Hermod.csproj" />
    <Project Path="libs/Hermod/HermodTests/HermodTests.csproj" />
    <Project Path="libs/Ratatoskr/Ratatoskr/Ratatoskr.csproj" />
    <Project Path="libs/Ratatoskr/RatatoskrTests/RatatoskrTests.csproj" />
    <Project Path="libs/Styx/Styx/Styx.csproj" />
    <Project Path="libs/Styx/StyxTests/StyxTests.csproj" />
  </Folder>
  <!--
    Not under Dependencies: nothing here builds against the console, it builds
    against this. It is in the solution because this checkout builds it against
    the Ratatoskr *this* repository pins, while its own clone builds it against
    the one it pins itself - and those two are not the same revision for as long
    as it takes somebody to move the second. That gap is not a nuisance, it is
    the early warning: three signature changes have turned up here first because
    of it, most recently OmemoSent (D110).

    (This comment used to say the console "reached sideways for a sibling since
    the submodules came out of it". They went back in - it pins Hermod, Styx and
    Ratatoskr again, so that a plain clone of it builds - and what makes the two
    trees differ is the pin, not the absence of one.)
  -->
  <Folder Name="/Console/">
    <Project Path="libs/XMPPConsole/XMPPConsole/XMPPConsole.csproj" />
    <Project Path="libs/XMPPConsole/XMPPConsole.Tests/XMPPConsole.Tests.csproj" />
  </Folder>
  <!--
    The second application, here for the same reason, with one consequence the
    console does not have: XMPPWebApp embeds a webpack frontend, and building it
    runs "npm ci" and "npm run build" unless -p:SkipFrontendBuild=true is given.
    So building THIS solution now needs npm on the machine, which it did not
    before. XMPPWebApp.Tests passes SkipFrontendBuild itself, but the embedding
    step still insists on a src/Frontend/dist that exists, so the frontend has to
    have been built once either way.

    Neither workflow is touched by that. ci.yml and nightly.yml both build
    XMPPConformanceTests/XMPPConformanceTests.csproj by name and never this file
    - a difference from the sibling suites that ci.yml explains where it makes
    it.

    It took a change over there to be buildable here at all: its two references
    named ..\..\libs\Ratatoskr and ..\..\libs\Hermod outright, and with the
    nested libs/ empty MSBuild skips a missing ProjectReference with a message
    rather than failing on it - then 452 errors about types those references
    would have brought. XMPPWebApp 23b2564 gives each one a conditional sibling,
    as XMPPConsole has carried since D97.
  -->
  <Folder Name="/WebApp/">
    <Project Path="libs/XMPPWebApp/src/XMPPWebApp/XMPPWebApp.csproj" />
    <Project Path="libs/XMPPWebApp/src/XMPPWebApp.Tests/XMPPWebApp.Tests.csproj" />
  </Folder>
  <Project Path="XMPPConformanceTests/XMPPConformanceTests.csproj" />
</Solution>
